  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Cross-Attention Fusion Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `CrossAttention(hidden, heads)`, multi-head cross-attention with separate `q` and `kv` projections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `CausalSelfAttention(hidden, heads)`, the masked self-attention from a standard decoder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `DecoderBlock`, composing the three sub-layers with pre-LN residuals."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `VisionLanguageDecoder`, four-layer decoder fed by a mock vision encoder output and a small text embedding table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `causal_mask(length)` returning a `(length, length)` lower-triangular boolean tensor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that feeds a batch of two text sequences of length 10 with image memory of length 197 and prints output shape, the self-attention mask shape, and the cross-attention output norm per position."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: decoder produces a `(2, 10, text_vocab)` logits tensor. Mask shape is `(10, 10)`. The KV-cache reuse check confirms identical logits between the cached and uncached paths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a learned tanh gate to the cross-attention residual (the Flamingo trick) and verify training converges from a near-zero initial gate. The gate starts at 0; the model recovers text-only behavior before mixing the image stream in.\n\n2. Implement interleaved attention where the same decoder consumes multiple images plus multiple text segments. Build the per-sample cross-attention mask that prevents text segment 2 from attending to image 1.\n\n3. Profile the cross-attention vs the self-attention layer at `Nt=64, Nv=576` (a 24x24 grid at higher resolution). The cross-attention cost is `Nt * Nv` and dominates at high image resolution.\n\n4. Add a query-side dropout on the cross-attention map and measure caption diversity on the demo (caption sample variance increases with dropout in the cross map).\n\n5. Swap the cross-attention layer for a Q-Former-style attention block where a fixed 32-token query pool attends to image features once per layer."
      ]
    }
  ],
